r Henry Gosson, […], published 1609, →OCLC, [Act II, scene ii]:"}, {"text": "Then he commenced to talk, really talk. and inside of two flaps of a herring's fin he had me mesmerized, like Eben Holt's boy at the town hall show. He talked about the ills of humanity, and the glories of health and Nature and service and land knows what all.", "reference": "1913, Joseph C[rosby] Lincoln, chapter IV, in Mr. Pratt’s Patients, New York, N.Y.; London: D[aniel] Appleton and Company, →OCLC:"}, {"text": "He's the only person I know who's going to vote at all. Most people have given up on politicians. After all, politicians have been promising to return us to the glory, wealth, and order of the twentieth century ever since I can remember.", "reference": "1993, Octavia Butler, chapter 3, in The Parable of the Sower:"}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "Worship or praise.", "tags": ["countable", "uncountable"], "examples": [], "quotes": [{"text": "Glory to God in the highest, and on earth peace, good will toward men.", "reference": "1611, The Holy Bible, […] (King James Version), London: […] Robert Barker, […], →OCLC, Luke 2:14:"}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [{"language": {"code": "hy", "name": "Armenian"}, "word": "փառք"}, {"language": {"code": "hy", "name": "Armenian"}, "word": "փառաբանություն"}, {"language": {"code": "nl", "name": "Dutch"}, "word": "lof"}, {"language": {"code": "nl", "name": "Dutch"}, "word": "dankzegging"}, {"language": {"code": "fi", "name": "Finnish"}, "word": "kunnia"}, {"language": {"code": "fr", "name": "French"}, "word": "gloire"}, {"language": {"code": "gl", "name": "Galician"}, "word": "groria"}, {"language": {"code": "gl", "name": "Galician"}, "word": "palma"}, {"language": {"code": "de", "name": "German"}, "word": "Rühmen"}, {"language": {"code": "de", "name": "German"}, "word": "Glorie"}, {"language": {"code": "el", "name": "Greek"}, "word": "δόξα"}, {"language": {"code": "hi"