e of God as perceived by humans in Abrahamic religions.", "tags": ["countable", "uncountable"], "examples": [], "quotes": [], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "(obsolete) Pride; boastfulness; arrogance.", "tags": ["countable", "obsolete", "uncountable"], "examples": [], "quotes": [{"text": "[…] But if thou declare\nThe Secrets, truth; and art so mad to dare\n(In glory of thy fortunes) to approue,\nThat rich-crownd Venus, mixt with thee in loue;\nIoue (fir’d with my aspersion, so dispred)\nWill, with a wreakefull lightning, dart thee dead.", "reference": "c. 1624, “A Hymne to Venus”, in George Chapman, transl., The Crowne of all Homers Workes Batrachomyomachia or the Battaile of Frogs and Mise, His Hymn’s and Epigrams, London: John Bill, page 106:"}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "Something glorious.", "tags": ["countable", "uncountable"], "examples": [], "quotes": [{"text": "It was a woman’s clothing, beyond a doubt, […] The two men gazed at the heap of feminine glories, — it might have been the most wonderful sight they ever had seen.", "reference": "1897, Richard Marsh, The Beetle:"}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}], "synonyms": ["halo", "praise", "worship", "fame", "honor", "honour"], "antonyms": []}, {"language": {"code": "en", "name": "English"}, "partOfSpeech": "verb", "pronunciations": [{"type": "ipa", "text": "/ˈɡlɔː.ɹi/", "tags": ["Received Pronunciation"]}, {"type": "ipa", "text": "/ˈɡloɹ.i/", "tags": ["Canada", "General American"]}, {"type": "ipa", "text": "[ˈɡlɔɹ.i]", "tags": ["Canada", "General American", "dialectal"]}, {"type": "ipa", "text": "/ˈɡloː.ɹi/", "tags": ["General Australian", "New Zealand"]}, {"type": "ipa", "text": "/ˈɡlo(ː)ɹi/", "tags": []}], "forms": [{"word": "glories", "tags": ["present", "singular", "third-person"]}, {"word": "glorying", "tags": ["participle", "present"]}, {"word": "gloried", "tags": ["participle", "past"]}, {"word": "gloried", "tags": ["past"]}], "senses": [{"definition": "To exult with joy; to rejoice.", "tags": [], "examples": [], "quotes": [{"text": "In what the Apostle did glory?—He gloried in a Cross. ... [T]o the Ear of a Galatian, it conveyed much the same Meaning, as if the Apostle had gloried in a Halter; gloried in the Gallows; gloried in a Gibbet.", "reference": "1753, James Hervey, A Visitation Sermon: Preached at Northampton, May 10, 1753:"}, {"text": "He says he glories in what happened, and that good may be done indirectly; but I wish he would not so wear himself out now he is getting old, and would leave such pigs to their wallowing.", "reference": "1891, Thomas Hardy, Tess of the d'Urbervilles:"}, {"text": "When the passion is extreme, suffering may actually be gloried in, provided it be for the ideal cause, death may lose its sting, the grave its victory.", "reference": "1902, William James, “Lectures 4 & 5”, in The Varieties of Religious Experience: A Study in Human Nature […] , New York, N.Y.; London: Longmans, Green, and Co. […], →OCLC:"}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [{"language": {"code": "bg", "name": "Bulgarian"}, "word": "радвам се"}, {"language": {"code": "bg", "name": "Bulgarian"}, "word": "ликувам"}, {"language": {"code": "de", "name": "German"}, "word": "jubilieren"}, {"language": {"code": "de", "name": "German"}, "word": "jubeln"}, {"language": {"code": "de", "name": "German"}, "word": "auskosten"}, {"language": {"code": "ja", "name": "Japanese"}, "word": "喜ぶ"}, {"language": {"code": "la", "name": "Latin"}, "word": "glōrior"}], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "To boast; to be proud.", "tags": [], "examples": ["For if in anything I have gloried to him on your behalf, I was not put to shame; but as we spake all things to you in truth, so our glorying also, which I made before Titus, was found to be truth."], "quotes": [], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [{"language": {"